{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FMapDirectCyclotomic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapDirectCyclotomic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FMapStructuralPaths","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ZBarParity"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uside_parity_never_descends_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uside_parity_never_descends_real","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapDirectCyclotomic.lean#L90-L98","doc":"**The odd fibre parity NEVER descends at a real substrate.** For every real\n`q` the u-side re-basing fails to transport the fibre bar-parity — it breaks\nalready at the `k = 1` odd rung (`q² ≠ −1`). Hence the odd (bar-odd, Q_β / S)\nchannel of the `c_k` is irreducibly *archimedean* at the substrate `q₀`, not a\nfibre cyclotomic re-basing — the exact KC17 conclusion, now machine-checked. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.sq_ne_neg_one_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.sq_ne_neg_one_real","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapDirectCyclotomic.lean#L83-L88","doc":"**No real substrate is ζ₄:** `q² = −1` is impossible over `ℝ` (`q² ≥ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uside_parity_descent_iff_zeta4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uside_parity_descent_iff_zeta4","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapDirectCyclotomic.lean#L73-L81","doc":"**Parity descent ⟺ ζ₄.** The u-side per-rung twist `(q²)^k` equals the q-side\nindex-parity `(−1)^k` for every rung `k` **iff** `q² = −1`. Forward: the\n`k = 1` (odd) rung already forces `q² = −1`; reverse: `(q²)^k = (−1)^k`\nfollows from `q² = −1` at every `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.direct_cyclotomic_fmap_valid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.direct_cyclotomic_fmap_valid","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapDirectCyclotomic.lean#L36-L51","doc":"The theorem asserting that the extraction algorithm correctly reconstructs the \nformal F-map while respecting the bar-parity constraint from `ZBarParity.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cyclotomicLadderExtract","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cyclotomicLadderExtract","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapDirectCyclotomic.lean#L27-L34","doc":"The Direct Cyclotomic functor mapping a formal sequence of integer polynomials \nto a sequence of ladder coefficients.\n\nThe algebraic root matching requires that the cyclotomic zeroes $u^k = 1$ \nof the Habiro basis map onto the inverse zeroes of the precision ladder $1 + c_k u^k$.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}